Package: lex1dx
Type: Package
Title: Fast 1-D k-Means with a 0.01% Relative Excess SSE Tolerance
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("N.", "Sriram",
           email = "comunaware@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Allan", "Gr\u00f8nlund",
           role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "Author of bundled kmeans1d wilber-interp solver")
  )
Description: Partitions one-dimensional numeric data into k contiguous clusters
    with a low within-cluster sum of squares. The default tuned pipeline sorts
    the data, collapses to M = max(4096, 32k) groups, runs a weighted
    wilber-interp dynamic program, and refines the cuts. Optional grouping
    to 0 through 9 significant digits (mode 'sig5' is an alias for sig 5) is
    provided, with a k-preserving fallback when grouping would leave fewer
    than k groups. An exact path, a choice of Fisher or wilber-interp solver,
    and optional observation weights are also provided. The C++17 core is
    shared with the 'Python' and 'Scala' implementations in the same
    repository. Method details are given in Sriram (2026)
    <doi:10.5281/zenodo.24543220>. Objectives and defaults differ from
    'lex1d', which remains the paper-faithful exact-quality reference.
